&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SALEM,&amp;nbsp;Ore.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:calibri,calibri_embeddedfont,calibri_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&mdash;&amp;nbsp;Oregon Housing and Community Services (OHCS) has been recognized&amp;nbsp;in&amp;nbsp;50 States, 50 Breakthroughs, an award&amp;nbsp;showcase highlighting the most innovative and impactful public-sector projects across the United States. The honor recognizes OHCS&rsquo; Oregon Centralized Application (ORCA), a first-of-its-kind&amp;nbsp;approach&amp;nbsp;of how affordable housing is funded in Oregon.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:calibri,calibri_embeddedfont,calibri_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
