          &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Passcode:&lt;/strong&gt; jP7xb2Ko&lt;/li&gt;
          &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Phone:&lt;/strong&gt; +1 503-446-4951&lt;/li&gt;
          &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Phone conference ID:&lt;/strong&gt; 336 777 99#&lt;/li&gt;
     &lt;/ul&gt;
     &lt;/li&gt;
     &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who:&lt;/strong&gt; Electronic Government Portal Advisory Board&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The Electronic Government Portal Advisory Board is established by &lt;a href="https://www.oregonlegislature.gov/bills_laws/ors/ors276a.html#:~:text=276A.270%20Definitions."&gt;ORS 276A.270-276&lt;/a&gt;. The board&rsquo;s primary function is to advise the State Chief Information Officer concerning the delivery of online services to the public.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The board is also charged with studying the digital information and service needs of Oregon residents, evaluating agencies&rsquo; effectiveness in using online portals, and considering further improvements in online portals.&lt;/p&gt;

